# DIAGNOSTICS

`vx: cpu: the node hung up` when the node holds another key or refuses this terminal, which it doesn't answer; `vx: cpu: <host>!<port>: Connection refused` when nothing listens.
It exits 0 when the node ends the session, 1 otherwise.

# BUGS

The exit status of rc on the node doesn't reach `vx cpu`'s.
Every cpu image vx makes on this machine carries the same node key, in plain, so every node booted from one answers as the same node; a node booted otherwise makes a key each boot, until keys are kept on disk.
A read of `dev/cons` that the node flushes has still taken the line typed, which is lost.
Symbolic links under <root> are followed, out of it too.
`net/` has no UDP and takes no calls: `announce`, `udp`, `ipifc` and `iproute` are refused, as `operation not supported`.
